This change allows for type aliases to be used for props of a component. Previously only `interface`s were being read by the documentation-framework for the purposes of generating prop tables.

Example:
```
/**
 * Hosts default wizard navigation logic by utilizing the wizard's context and WizardNav/WizardNavItem.
 * This component is not exposed to consumers.
 */

type WizardNavInternalProps = {
  /** Some nav prop description */
  nav: Partial<WizardNavProps>;
  /** Some isNavExpanded description */
  isNavExpanded: boolean;
} & {
  /** Some other prop description */
  someOtherProp?: Partial<WizardStepProps>;
} & {
  /** Wow, another? cool */
  wowAnotherProp?: WizardBasicStep;
};
```

